DESCRIPTION:Titan’s dense atmosphere conceals a remarkably Earth-like la
 ndscape shaped by dunes\, rivers\, lakes\, seas\, and possible remnants of
  past hydrologic environments. The Cassini RADAR investigation provided ou
 r first detailed view of this surface and enabled measurements extending w
 ell beyond imaging. In this talk\, I will review how radar sounding was us
 ed to measure the depths and constrain the composition of Titan’s northe
 rn seas\, as well as how Cassini’s bistatic radar observations are revea
 ling t\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-09-20 09:42 PDT
LOCATION:Mitchell Earth Sciences
END:VEVENT
